mmary type="html">The UN migration agency has reported that at least 139 people were killed and 84 remain missing after a migrant boat sank overnight on its way to Yemen. At least 80 Ethiopians survived the incident but 15 children died.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Eritrea urges UN deterrence measures against Ethiopia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7f10178dd2367a6f2c7673edbaaee11a9127e747cf31f30fa516a0550e053407</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T18:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eritrea-urges-un-deterrence-measures-against-ethiopia/a-79629670--3be24e605304.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eritrea-urges-un-deterrence-measures-against-ethiopia/a-79629670?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Eritrea has officially requested UN Security Council assistance over the conflict in Tigray. Both Eritrea and Ethiopia accuse each other of fueling regional instability.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>South Sudan's road to elections remains uncertain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2f09c0afacb8321ae29dbd6f760cd125010a9c28556e0c41b65b3a4ea1a5a98</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T04:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-sudan-s-road-to-elections-remains-uncertain/a-79563442--6016ef79f3a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-sudan-s-road-to-elections-remains-uncertain/a-79563442?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Sudan's first general election is set for December 22. Insecurity, political tensions and the failure to begin voter registration have raised doubts over whether a credible poll can be held.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Anthropic report: Is Russia using AI for disinformation in the Central African Republic and elsewhere across Africa?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:735d473d877d87701f83407f108df0e63df8216b7eccc8c86cc6e55571ca4725</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T17:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/anthropic-report-is-russia-using-ai-for-disinformation-in-the-central-african-republic-and-elsewhere/a-79476947--316a6e450389.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/anthropic-report-is-russia-using-ai-for-disinformation-in-the-central-african-republic-and-elsewhere-across-africa/a-79476947?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An Anthropic report says the AI model Claude was used in pro-Russian campaigns in the Central African Republic. Similar allegations were raised for the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Kenya, Sudan and Mali.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>Morocco's first female head of government: Symbol or real reform?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:696bee2c524dcb5f8433da2441c55109e255a63e7f2f43ec1c863fd4a94b5790</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T08:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/morocco-s-first-female-head-of-government-symbol-or-real-reform/a-79521808--5c6131d5d637.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/morocco-s-first-female-head-of-government-symbol-or-real-reform/a-79521808?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fatima Zahra Mansouri has been chosen as Morocco's first female prime minister. Is her appointment a kind of symbolism, to show Morocco in a positive light? Or could Mansouri bring genuine changes for Moroccan women?</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry></feed>
